1
00:02:47,272 --> 00:02:53,272
How do they solve a mystery when they don't have a clue?

2
00:05:34,545 --> 00:05:40,545
Looney Tunes: Back in Action is a animation, comedy,
family film directed by Joe Dante.

3
00:08:21,818 --> 00:08:27,818
Fed up with all the attention going to Bugs Bunny, Daffy Duck quits
Hollywood, teams up with recently-fired stuntman Damien Drake Jr.

4
00:11:09,090 --> 00:11:15,090
and embarks on a round-the-world adventure, along
with Bugs and The VP of Warner Bros.

5
00:13:56,363 --> 00:14:02,363
Their mission?

6
00:16:43,636 --> 00:16:49,636
Find Damien's father, and the missing blue diamond...

7
00:19:30,909 --> 00:19:36,909
and stay one step ahead of The Acme Corp., who wants
the diamond for their own purposes.

8
00:22:18,181 --> 00:22:24,181
DJ Drake / Tasmanian Devil (voice) / She-Devil
(voice) / Self, played by Brendan Fraser.

9
00:25:05,454 --> 00:25:11,454
Kate, played by Jenna Elfman.

10
00:27:52,727 --> 00:27:58,727
Mr. Chairman, played by Steve Martin.

11
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Bugs Bunny-Daffy Duck / Beaky Buzzard / Sylvester /
Mama Bear (voice), played by Joe Alaskey.

12
00:33:27,272 --> 00:33:33,272
Yosemite Sam / Foghorn Leghorn / Nasty Canasta (voice), played by Jeff Bennett.

13
00:36:14,545 --> 00:36:20,545
Damien Drake, played by Timothy Dalton.

14
00:39:01,818 --> 00:39:07,818
Looney Tunes: Back in Action is a 2003 American live-action animated
comedy film directed by Joe Dante and written by Larry Doyle.

15
00:41:49,090 --> 00:41:55,090
The film stars Brendan Fraser, Jenna Elfman and Steve Martin, with Timothy
Dalton, Joan Cusack, and Heather Locklear in supporting roles.

16
00:44:36,363 --> 00:44:42,363
A parody of action and spy films, the plot follows Looney Tunes characters Bugs Bunny and Daffy Duck as they become intertwined in a plot by
the Acme Corporation's chairman to transform the world's population into subservient monkeys using the Blue Monkey diamond.

17
00:47:23,636 --> 00:47:29,636
They accompany aspiring stuntman DJ Drake and Warner Bros.

18
00:50:10,909 --> 00:50:16,909
executive Kate Houghton on their journey to thwart the chairman's plot, which
doubles as a mission to rescue the former's abducted father, Damian.

19
00:52:58,181 --> 00:53:04,181
The film was the result of multiple attempts by Warner Bros.

20
00:55:45,454 --> 00:55:51,454
to develop a sequel to Space Jam (1996).

21
00:58:32,727 --> 00:58:38,727
It was originally produced as Spy Jam, which was
intended to star Jackie Chan in the lead role.

22
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
Dante, out of a personal dislike for Space Jam, substantially developed the project to more closely represent the original personalities
of the Looney Tunes characters, with Walt Disney Animation Studios animator Eric Goldberg serving as animation director.

23
01:04:07,272 --> 01:04:13,272
However, Dante reportedly had no creative control on the project, and
the final film became different from what he intended.

24
01:06:54,545 --> 01:07:00,545
The film was the last project by Warner Bros.

25
01:09:41,818 --> 01:09:47,818
Feature Animation and the final film scored by composer and Dante collaborator Jerry Goldsmith, who died
eight months following its release; John Debney composed additional material for the score.

26
01:12:29,090 --> 01:12:35,090
Looney Tunes: Back in Action premiered on November 9, 2003, and was
theatrically released in the United States on November 14.

27
01:15:16,363 --> 01:15:22,363
The film received mixed reviews from critics and was a box-office
failure, grossing $68 million on an $80 million budget.

28
01:18:03,636 --> 01:18:09,636
Due to the film's financial failure, Warner Bros.

29
01:20:50,909 --> 01:20:56,909
subsequently canceled several planned Looney Tunes
projects, including new theatrical short films.

30
01:23:38,181 --> 01:23:44,181
At the 31st Annie Awards, the film was nominated for four
Annie Awards, including Best Animated Feature.

31
01:26:25,454 --> 01:26:31,454
The film explores themes of diamond, bunny, spy, movie business, duck.

32
01:29:12,727 --> 01:29:18,727
The tone is lighthearted.
